            <div xml:id="d715">

                <pb facs="0801" n="681" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg681"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01 Foreign Control/94: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-19T11:00:00-05:00">March 19, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>75. Reber’s No. 70, March 11, 3 p.m., and Department’s 66, March 12, 2
                        p.m.<anchor n="41" xml:id="d715-f1"/> The Finance Corporation states that no
                    request for funds for sanitation for the use of Dr. Howells and/or other medical
                    officer designated by the International Committee has been received from the
                    Liberian Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d715-f1" n="41" xml:id="d715-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed.</p>
